META-INF/
build27/

# build staging and JavaFX natives — never commit these
fat/
gameclasses/
jfx27/
*.dll
saves/

# JVM crash dumps. The Robot tests abort under load - a SIGABRT, documented in the release notes as known
# flakiness - and each one leaves a 1,480-line crash log at the repository root. Two of them were COMMITTED before
# this line existed, which is how a release repository ends up carrying its own crash reports.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# The same class as the crash logs above, and the reason a rule is worth having even when one instance is already
# covered: THREE BUILD ARTEFACTS WERE TRACKED IN THIS RELEASE REPOSITORY, each regenerable and none of them
# referenced by the pom, the scripts, the docs or the source - measured with grep before removing them.
#
#   javafx-swt.jar             36 KB, an SWT bridge nothing here uses
#   dependency-reduced-pom.xml written by maven-shade-plugin on every build (the plugin is in pom.xml)
#   fjerr.log                  a JavaFX startup warning from 2026-09-23
#
# `hs_err_pid*.log` was already ignored because two crash logs had been committed; `fjerr.log` is a log too, and it
# slipped past a rule that named ONE KIND of log rather than logs.
*.log
javafx-swt.jar
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
